[{:seon.task/name "a-real-model-run-meets-the-conflict-a-scenario-names"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: `seon.fixtures/scenarios` `:hairy`'s tasks a and b carry no `:plan`, so what makes their merge conflict (a writes `(+ x K)`, b writes `(+ K x)`) lives only in the scripted model's replies. Reproduction: `bin/check e2e scenario hairy model` (DeepSeek): a real model wrote the same text for both, `:conflicts-measured 0`, `:attached-tasks 0`, and it passed without a hairy merge. Correct: a scenario that expects conflicts states in each task's `:plan` the body text that makes them differ, as `:conflict`'s plans do (`app.m/f` as `(+ x 1)` and `(inc x)`), so a real model run meets the conflicts the scenario is named for. The default plan from `seon.fixtures/decls` stays for scenarios that need none."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.e2e-test/a-real-model-run-meets-the-conflict-a-scenario-names}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-run-with-no-agent-is-not-reused"
  :seon.task/plan "Found in RESUME's follow-ups (2026-10-22), and picked as step E's first request (design -> implement -> merge, worked by Seon agents on a worktree's own root): `seon.e2e/agents-reused` counts `:seon.run/agent` with `frequencies` over every run of `seon.task/runs`. A run refused before its spawn has no agent (`seon.task/run-start-tx` takes a nil agent), so two refused runs answer `[nil]`: the scenario reports a reused agent that never existed, and its check reads a refused spawn as a reuse. Correct: only runs that had an agent are counted; agents-reused of a db whose runs are two agentless refused spawns and two runs with distinct agents is `[]`, and of one where two runs share agent `:a1` is `[:a1]`. The proof builds its db as `seon.e2e-test/turns-count-the-work-runs` does (`seon.test-store/test-db`, `seon.task/create-tx`, `seon.task/run-start-tx`). Size: one line in `seon.e2e/agents-reused`, one deftest."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.e2e-test/a-run-with-no-agent-is-not-reused}}]
